[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194484] [:db/retract 17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194485] [:db/retract 17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194486] [:db/retract 17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194487] [:db/retract 17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194488] [:db/retract 17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194436] [:db/retract 17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194437] [:db/retract 17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194438] [:db/retract 17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194439] [:db/retract 17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194440] {:db/id 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" "question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" "question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198642 :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}-2y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2y)=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2(0) & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194483 :answer-field/correct "answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" "answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" "answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" "answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" "answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/id #uuid "ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/id #uuid "fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/id #uuid "d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/id #uuid "f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/id #uuid "64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198634 :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194435 :answer-field/correct "answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" "answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" "answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" "answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" "answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/id #uuid "e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/id #uuid "a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/id #uuid "e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/id #uuid "2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/id #uuid "ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/id #uuid "e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163107" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y-x \\\\ {e}^{x+y} \\\\ {x}^{2}+y\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} \\\\ \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & {e}^{x+y} \\\\ 2x & \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)=-1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-x)=1, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y}, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ {e}^{x+y} & {e}^{x+y} \\\\ 2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, the missing entries are $1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" "answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" "answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" "answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" "answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" :answer/id #uuid "5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" :answer/id #uuid "ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $2y$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" :answer/id #uuid "4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1,\\,$ $y{e}^{x+y},$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" :answer/id #uuid "a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1,\\,$ $y{e}^{x+y},$ and $2y$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer/id #uuid "a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/id #uuid "233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/math-academy-id "q-163051" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/id #uuid "35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer-field/choices ["answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" "answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" "answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" "answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" "answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer/id #uuid "22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" :answer/id #uuid "2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & \\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" :answer/id #uuid "0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" :answer/id #uuid "55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a" :answer/id #uuid "8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/id #uuid "41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163071" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={e}^{x+{y}^{2}},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+{y}^{2}})={e}^{x+{y}^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+{y}^{2}})=2y{e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+{y}^{2}} & 2y{e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-1=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+1+2=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f7594d4-8ebb-59a3-b3a9-1b3956c96f5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee" "answer-dc58ca95-eb79-5822-8857-92d798da6418" "answer-b96dff26-09a1-53b6-80bd-bf9b4effbbec" "answer-2f7594d4-8ebb-59a3-b3a9-1b3956c96f5b" "answer-9a750e94-0425-5e6a-9e86-ff988b0a821f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee" :answer/id #uuid "e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc58ca95-eb79-5822-8857-92d798da6418" :answer/id #uuid "dc58ca95-eb79-5822-8857-92d798da6418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b96dff26-09a1-53b6-80bd-bf9b4effbbec" :answer/id #uuid "b96dff26-09a1-53b6-80bd-bf9b4effbbec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f7594d4-8ebb-59a3-b3a9-1b3956c96f5b" :answer/id #uuid "2f7594d4-8ebb-59a3-b3a9-1b3956c96f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a750e94-0425-5e6a-9e86-ff988b0a821f" :answer/id #uuid "9a750e94-0425-5e6a-9e86-ff988b0a821f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198636 :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=0,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-0=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+1=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194447 :answer-field/correct 17592186194449 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/id #uuid "bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/math-academy-id "q-163115" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})=\\frac{2}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})=\\frac{1}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2})=2,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2})=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} & \\frac{1}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+5=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" "answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" "answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" "answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" "answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" :answer/id #uuid "0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" :answer/id #uuid "04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" :answer/id #uuid "2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer/id #uuid "d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191" :answer/id #uuid "be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/id #uuid "e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163117" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡6\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡6+0+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6=\\operatorname{sin}⁡6+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7824eaf9-cd23-55b4-9fd6-76d9b52cc30d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1b5a290-a6c3-5e27-ae81-c0fb5e23fb17" "answer-fea47a30-e99a-5e73-998f-db22092d213e" "answer-f3e53c85-f2b8-58f8-8b33-f1eca57834dc" "answer-ba23c5ce-b11d-501d-b14c-4c4d08d14c26" "answer-7824eaf9-cd23-55b4-9fd6-76d9b52cc30d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1b5a290-a6c3-5e27-ae81-c0fb5e23fb17" :answer/id #uuid "c1b5a290-a6c3-5e27-ae81-c0fb5e23fb17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fea47a30-e99a-5e73-998f-db22092d213e" :answer/id #uuid "fea47a30-e99a-5e73-998f-db22092d213e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3e53c85-f2b8-58f8-8b33-f1eca57834dc" :answer/id #uuid "f3e53c85-f2b8-58f8-8b33-f1eca57834dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡4+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba23c5ce-b11d-501d-b14c-4c4d08d14c26" :answer/id #uuid "ba23c5ce-b11d-501d-b14c-4c4d08d14c26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡5+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7824eaf9-cd23-55b4-9fd6-76d9b52cc30d" :answer/id #uuid "7824eaf9-cd23-55b4-9fd6-76d9b52cc30d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡6+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199488 :tutorial/content "The equation of the tangent plane to a surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0),$ where $z_0=f(x_0,y_0),$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0).\n$$\n\nLet's express this equation in terms of the total derivative.\n\nWriting our multivariable function $f:\\mathbb R^2 \\to \\mathbb R$ as $f\\left(\\mathbf x \\right),$ where ![](images/88/88f9f758bffba384670449973c5c89edae05c67268d2914a12801b21b60a319f.svg) the total derivative of $f$ is given by\n\n![](images/56/56dc34676135e9c35b9e08cff732715c5d878d4a19f4fee6625384460ed6ee5f.svg)\n\nLet ![](images/ca/ca5b0074c216a3235f015d7b96dece9ffc6fc50eecbdd0b5e97dfbd89eb446fa.svg) Then, we can re-write the equation of the tangent plane as a matrix equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-{z}_{0} & =(x-{x}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) \\\\ z-{z}_{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x-{x}_{0} \\\\ y-{y}_{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z-f({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}]\\cdot ([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{0} \\\\ {y}_{0}\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ z-f(a) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(a) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(a)\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (x-a) \\\\ z-f(a) & ={f}^{′}(a)(x-a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane to $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf{a},$ in matrix form, is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186198642 :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}-2y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"] [17592186198642 :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2y)=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2(0) & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] [17592186198642 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/id #uuid "ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be"] ["answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/id #uuid "fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019"] ["answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/id #uuid "d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea"] ["answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/id #uuid "f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b"] ["answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/id #uuid "64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9"] ["answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/correct "answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices "answer-ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices "answer-fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices "answer-d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices "answer-f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b"] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices "answer-64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9"] [17592186198634 :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$"] [17592186198634 :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] [17592186198634 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/id #uuid "e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499"] ["answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2x\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/id #uuid "a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702"] ["answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/id #uuid "e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146"] ["answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/id #uuid "2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794"] ["answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/id #uuid "ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb"] ["answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/correct "answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices "answer-e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices "answer-a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices "answer-e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices "answer-2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794"] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices "answer-ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/id #uuid "e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163107"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y-x \\\\ {e}^{x+y} \\\\ {x}^{2}+y\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} \\\\ \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & {e}^{x+y} \\\\ 2x & \\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)=-1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-x)=1, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y}, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ {e}^{x+y} & {e}^{x+y} \\\\ 2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, the missing entries are $1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1.$"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2"] ["answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" :answer/id #uuid "5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e"] ["answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e" :answer/value "$-1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1$"] ["answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" :answer/id #uuid "ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574"] ["answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574" :answer/value "$-1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $2y$"] ["answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" :answer/id #uuid "4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3"] ["answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3" :answer/value "$1,\\,$ $y{e}^{x+y},$ and $1$"] ["answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" :answer/id #uuid "a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd"] ["answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd" :answer/value "$1,\\,$ $y{e}^{x+y},$ and $2y$"] ["answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer/id #uuid "a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5"] ["answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5" :answer/value "$1,\\,$ ${e}^{x+y},$ and $1$"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/correct "answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/choices "answer-5ab7b9b5-4008-5e6e-8865-0f92a0579f0e"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/choices "answer-ac0d31a6-90de-5ed5-abf3-0ec64309b574"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/choices "answer-4e6d2172-6c9d-5544-87e6-2d6bfa9d6ce3"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/choices "answer-a937722a-014a-5b62-9578-a0d76b204dbd"] ["answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2" :answer-field/choices "answer-a2e0fd02-52d6-5108-b58e-81e5f92525e5"] ["question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0742372b-5487-5dd8-bf84-219c793b3af2"] [17592186198412 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e4c8c472-15d1-572f-9440-48aac06cd29f"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/id #uuid "233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/math-academy-id "q-163051"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/id #uuid "35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409"] ["answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer/id #uuid "22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902"] ["answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" :answer/id #uuid "2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a"] ["answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & \\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" :answer/id #uuid "0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf"] ["answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" :answer/id #uuid "55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f"] ["answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a" :answer/id #uuid "8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a"] ["answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/correct "answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/choices "answer-22517a46-9e06-5b23-9c60-a096babd6902"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/choices "answer-2ef889ac-2980-5e6c-98ea-cb7cf876863a"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b47e061-fca8-5295-adef-032c9c071ddf"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/choices "answer-55b220b0-4440-5962-b48e-b368d091875f"] ["answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409" :answer-field/choices "answer-8f3826df-e89c-574b-869e-aafefa7eef5a"] ["question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-35fee1ea-d13a-5c7a-abbe-6f0b8b9ab409"] [17592186198412 :knowledge-point/questions "question-233a01ce-8236-503f-8343-bf44a66e9626"] ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/id #uuid "41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c"] ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163071"] ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={e}^{x+{y}^{2}},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"] ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+{y}^{2}})={e}^{x+{y}^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+{y}^{2}})=2y{e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+{y}^{2}} & 2y{e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-1=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+1+2=4.\n$$"] ["question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c"] ["answer-e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee" :answer/id #uuid "e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee"] ["answer-e23686e8-e6e0-5d6f-9b01-569d4870e8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e23686