b292b55c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ac4ab69d-722b-5430-b62d-48dc3d21f50c"] [17592186198413 :knowledge-point/questions "question-41ff97cf-642e-5207-833e-62b8b292b55c"] [17592186198636 :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"] [17592186198636 :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=0,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-0=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+1=3.\n$$"] [17592186198636 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186194447 :answer-field/correct 17592186194449] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/id #uuid "bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680"] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/math-academy-id "q-163115"] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})=\\frac{2}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})=\\frac{1}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2})=2,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2})=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} & \\frac{1}{2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}} \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+5=7.\n$$"] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816"] ["answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" :answer/id #uuid "0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38"] ["answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" :answer/id #uuid "04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7"] ["answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" :answer/id #uuid "2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf"] ["answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer/id #uuid "d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2"] ["answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2" :answer/value "7"] ["answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191" :answer/id #uuid "be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191"] ["answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/correct "answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/choices "answer-0ec31ce9-c00a-5bd1-8daf-af84138f2b38"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/choices "answer-04006744-1bae-5bb4-accb-e390d3f45ea7"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/choices "answer-2c6b6852-32ef-51ce-9d42-6fe9f0a29caf"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/choices "answer-d7c6cb25-2f85-50fe-b3a9-1118046f2bf2"] ["answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816" :answer-field/choices "answer-be150c75-3596-5565-b705-b3e774648191"] ["question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7ae93f63-1fd3-519e-8190-4b93e47d0816"] [17592186198414 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bc54e1e5-dbca-5fc5-bf13-79bd1c80e680"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/id #uuid "e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163117"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}_{2})=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡6\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡6+0+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6=\\operatorname{sin}⁡6+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6.\n$$"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8"] ["answer-c1b5a290-a6c3-5e27-ae81-c0fb5e23fb17" :answer/id #uuid "c1b5a290-a6c3-5e27-ae81-c0fb5