8" :answer-field/choices "answer-ba23c5ce-b11d-501d-b14c-4c4d08d14c26"] ["answer-field-c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8" :answer-field/choices "answer-7824eaf9-cd23-55b4-9fd6-76d9b52cc30d"] ["question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c2600867-21b3-5594-bb4f-ca47a76745c8"] [17592186198414 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e574592a-62af-5f54-90e2-87d7393db0a8"] [17592186199488 :tutorial/content "The equation of the tangent plane to a surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0),$ where $z_0=f(x_0,y_0),$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0).\n$$\n\nLet's express this equation in terms of the total derivative.\n\nWriting our multivariable function $f:\\mathbb R^2 \\to \\mathbb R$ as $f\\left(\\mathbf x \\right),$ where ![](images/88/88f9f758bffba384670449973c5c89edae05c67268d2914a12801b21b60a319f.svg) the total derivative of $f$ is given by\n\n![](images/56/56dc34676135e9c35b9e08cff732715c5d878d4a19f4fee6625384460ed6ee5f.svg)\n\nLet ![](images/ca/ca5b0074c216a3235f015d7b96dece9ffc6fc50eecbdd0b5e97dfbd89eb446fa.svg) Then, we can re-write the equation of the tangent plane as a matrix equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-{z}_{0} & =(x-{x}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) \\\\ z-{z}_{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x-{x}_{0} \\\\ y-{y}_{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z-f({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}]\\cdot ([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{0} \\\\ {y}_{0}\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ z-f(a) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(a) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(a)\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (x-a) \\\\ z-f(a) & ={f}^{′}(a)(x-a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane to $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf{a},$ in matrix form, is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$"]] "retractions" [[17592186198642 :question/problem "For the transformation $f: R^{2} → R$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = x^{2} - 2y, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\ncalculate $f^{′}$ at $a = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194484] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194485] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194486] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194487] [17592186194483 :answer-field/choices 17592186194488] [17592186198634 :question/problem "For the function $f: R^{2} → R$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = x^{2} + y^{2}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\ncalculate $f^{′}(x)$."] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194436] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194437] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194438] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194439] [17592186194435 :answer-field/choices 17592186194440] [17592186198636 :question/problem "Consider the function $f: R^{2} → R$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = x^{2} + y, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$z - ∗ = \\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix})$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"] [17592186199488 :tutorial/content "The equation of the tangent plane to a surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0),$ where $z_0=f(x_0,y_0),$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0).\n$$\n\nLet's express this equation in terms of the total derivative.\n\nWriting our multivariable function $f:\\mathbb R^2 \\to \\mathbb R$ as $f\\left(\\mathbf x \\right),$ where ![](images/88/88f9f758bffba384670449973c5c89edae05c67268d2914a12801b21b60a319f.svg) the total derivative of $f$ is given by\n\n![](images/56/56dc34676135e9c35b9e08cff732715c5d878d4a19f4fee6625384460ed6ee5f.svg)\n\nLet ![](images/ca/ca5b0074c216a3235f015d7b96dece9ffc6fc50eecbdd0b5e97dfbd89eb446fa.svg) Then, we can re-write the equation of the tangent plane as a matrix equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-{z}_{0} & =(x-{x}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\cdot \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) \\\\ z-{z}_{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x-{x}_{0} \\\\ y-{y}_{0}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ z-f({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot (\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{0} \\\\ {y}_{0}\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ z-f(a) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(a) & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(a)\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot (x-a) \\\\ z-f(a) & ={f}^{′}(a)(x-a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane to $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf{a},$ in matrix form, is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$"]]}]